# chart-content-after-version.allow - charts whose files changed after their version was set,
# where the published version is proven to hold the change, or the change is proven not to
# alter what any Sovereign runs. Read by scripts/check-chart-content-after-version.py from the
# commit it judges (#7922).
#
# One entry per line: <chart folder> <version> <through commit, 40 hex> <reason>
# An entry covers its chart only while the chart is at <version> and no commit after <through>
# changed the chart's files. The next change to the chart ends it: the release writer then
# publishes a new version, and the check names the entry as one to delete.
#
# Before FND-029 (#7889, 15 November 2026) a release run published a chart's version again
# with other files. Each chart below was last changed by a commit whose own release run
# packaged and pushed that same version from that commit, so the published version holds
# every change the check lists. Evidence: the run of Blueprint Release named in the entry, its
# job "build (<chart folder minus /chart>)" and its step "Helm push to GHCR". Since FND-029 a
# version is never published again with other files.

# Run 43665853442 (workflow_dispatch from build-continuum-controller.yaml) checked out this
# commit and pushed bp-continuum:0.2.1, digest sha256:5804b6dee774be809b5e8eb3d9438d4756fb9a693444f73d4ef723e0ec33670b,
# at 2026-11-15T02:24:35Z. No later run built products/continuum.
products/continuum/chart 0.2.1 dd54d5e8eeaebb9fedebcf20c8d5fbd5b25e2b68 published 0.2.1 was packaged from this commit (run 43665853442); the 13 later commits are image-tag bumps, all in it

